# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles run inside Linux containers - they must always
# have LF line endings regardless of the checkout platform. Without this, a
# Windows checkout (autocrlf) silently converts docker-entrypoint.sh back to
# CRLF on every git operation, which breaks the container's #!/bin/sh shebang
# and crashes it at startup - this exact bug cost real debugging time before
# being traced back to autocrlf rather than the file content itself.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
